 "section_summary": "This section comprises U.S. Political Adviser for Japan Despatch No. 731 (November 16, 1948) and the first 56 pages of an enclosed SCAP Civil Information and Education Section special report, 'Roster and Statistics of Japanese Educational Institutions, April and November 1946, Part 7: Fukuoka Prefecture.' The report provides an introductory overview of the Japanese educational administrative hierarchy, jurisdiction, and school reorganization, followed by twelve comprehensive statistical tables detailing institutions, student enrollments, and teaching staff across higher, secondary, elementary, and special education levels as of April and November 1946. It then presents the opening portion of the prefecture's detailed school roster, covering national, prefectural, and municipal institutions down through municipal elementary schools.",
